WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:06.109
- I cook for warthogs,
emu, lions, tigers, hyenas,

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:09.609
spoonbill, sun bear, flamingo and giraffe.

00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:13.399
They can be very picky.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.196
Every morning, I am preparing
around 350 pounds of food.

00:00:19.196 --> 00:00:20.661
My name is Stacy Kyles,
and I prepare the food

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:23.755
for the animals at the Oakland Zoo.

00:00:23.755 --> 00:00:26.422
I'm also known as the zoo chef.

00:00:29.794 --> 00:00:34.051
My day starts off very early,
before the sun even comes up.

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:35.650
I've gotta get the food for the animals,

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.101
or we have nothing to prepare.

00:00:37.101 --> 00:00:38.487
- [Radio DJ] Showers
across northern California.

00:00:38.487 --> 00:00:42.861
- The calm before the storm
of getting to the market.

00:00:42.861 --> 00:00:45.840
I need to get about a ton of food today,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.323
literally.

00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:48.376
(exhales)

00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:50.707
The produce market's kind of hectic.

00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:53.084
You've got a lot of forklifts
running back and forth.

00:00:53.084 --> 00:00:55.458
You've got trucks everywhere.

00:00:55.458 --> 00:00:58.146
There's a lot to choose from.

00:00:58.146 --> 00:01:01.132
I have to stay organized, or
this can get very overwhelming.

00:01:01.132 --> 00:01:03.378
I've got a huge market
that I've gotta go through,

00:01:03.378 --> 00:01:05.020
I've gotta pick out the right produce,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.589
so I've got a limited amount
of time at the market,

00:01:07.589 --> 00:01:11.756
because I have to get back
here to prepare the diets.

00:01:13.455 --> 00:01:15.815
I open the door to the
kitchen, and then I know

00:01:15.815 --> 00:01:17.732
my day has truly begun.

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:22.361
(light operatic music)

00:01:26.198 --> 00:01:28.281
Sun bears, 48 grams apple.

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:34.230
Coatimundi, three
hard-boiled eggs cut in half.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.141
Lions, 10 bones and five—
Twenty ounces of grapes off the vine—

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:39.886
Seven servings— 
—and two whole bananas

00:01:39.886 --> 00:01:42.291
60 grams of crickets, one drop vitamin E—

00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:46.458
44 grams banana (Stacy's
voiceovers overlapping each other).

00:01:48.535 --> 00:01:50.974
The zoo itself as a whole prepares about

00:01:50.974 --> 00:01:52.642
a thousand diets a day.

00:01:52.642 --> 00:01:54.653
So that's anywhere from the elephants down

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:57.883
to the leafcutter ants
and all the little reptiles

00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.966
and all the little frogs.

00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:05.481
(lively instrumental music)

00:02:05.481 --> 00:02:07.160
it's important that we get the diets right

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.400
because the animals
can't send the food back.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.331
They can't tell us, oh I don't like this.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:13.917
We don't take days off.

00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:15.296
Everything still has to happen.

00:02:15.296 --> 00:02:18.065
The food get prepared exactly the same way

00:02:18.065 --> 00:02:19.587
every single day.

00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:21.173
I tried telling them
it was Christmas once,

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:22.614
they didn't pay attention.

00:02:22.614 --> 00:02:26.281
(lively instrumental music)

